{"name":"Steam Bath","hex":"#ccd0da","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steam bath","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A room or building filled with steam, in which people sit and sweat.","The act of bathing by exposure to steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam_bath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steam bath","blocks":[{"text":"A steam bath is a steam-filled room or steam-filled cabinet designed for the purpose of relaxation and holistic treatment. Steam baths have been formally recognized since ancient Greek and Roman times, yet variations can be found throughout the Middle East, Asia, Mesoamerica, and Northern Africa. The Greeks developed early vapor baths called laconica in Sparta, while the Roman variation was referred to as thermae, among the most famous of which is located in Bath, England, and was founded in the first century AD."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Ba%C3%B1os_Romanos%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_39-41_HDR.JPG/330px-Ba%C3%B1os_Romanos%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_39-41_HDR.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_bath","wikidata":"Q718955"},{"title":"Steam","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is water vapor, often mixed with air and/or an aerosol of liquid water droplets. This may occur by evaporation or by boiling, where heat is applied until water reaches the enthalpy of vaporization. Superheated or saturated steam is invisible; however, wet steam, a visible mist or aerosol of water droplets, is often referred to as \"steam\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg/330px-Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam","wikidata":"Q3251738"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Roman_baths.png/500px-Roman_baths.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Roman_baths.png/1280px-Roman_baths.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Roman_baths.png/500px-Roman_baths.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artist's depiction of a traditional Roman thermae.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoman_baths.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Kusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_%2813%29.jpg/500px-Kusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_%2813%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Kusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_%2813%29.jpg/1280px-Kusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_%2813%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Kusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_%2813%29.jpg/500px-Kusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_%2813%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kusatsu Onsen, a hot springs resort, located in Japan's Gunma Prefecture.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKusatsu_Onsen%2C_Gunma_Prefecture%3B_November_2018_(13).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/1280px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki